{{also|zusammen-}}
==German==

===Etymology===

From {{inh|de|gmh|[[zesamene]], [[zesamne]], [[zesamen]]||together}}, from {{inh|de|goh|zisamane||together}}. From {{prefix|de|zu|t1=to|sammen||t2=together}} (these days, {{m|de|sammen}} is only found in compounds), form {{der|de|gem-pro|*samana||together}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*sem-||together, one}}. Cognate with {{cog|enm|to-samen||together}}. Related to obsolete {{cog|en|sam||together}}, whose earlier form was {{m|en|samen}}.

{{cog|nl|tezamen||together}} has been formed in a similar fashion, with its contracted form being {{m|nl|samen}} and its ancestral form {{m|dum|tsamen}}. Also cognate with {{cog|sco|samin||together}}, {{cog|da|sammen||together}}, {{cog|sv|samman||together}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tsuˈzamən/|[tsuˈzamən]|[tsuˈzamm̩]|lang=de}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|/tsəˈzamən/|lang=de}} {{a|colloquial variant}}
* {{IPA|/ˈtsam(ən)/|lang=de}} {{a|Bavaria, Austria; chiefly colloquial}}
* {{audio|De-zusammen.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{hyphenation|zu|sam|men|lang=de}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[together]]
#* '''1903''', {{w|Fanny zu Reventlow}}, ''[[s:de:Ellen Olestjerne|Ellen Olestjerne]]'', in ''Franziska Gräfin zu Reventlow: Gesammelte Werke'', Albert Langen, page 526:
#*: Trotz all dieser Bitternisse war es noch ein wunderbar schöner Sommer, den die drei Freunde '''zusammen''' verlebten.
#*:: Despite all these bitter feelings, it was yet a wonderfully beautiful summer, which the three friends spent together.

